onent":"JAX","home":false,"pf":34.0,"pa":31.0,"off_snaps":59,"epa_per_play":0.2246,"pass_rate":0.5763,"pass_rate_neutral":0.6304,"def_epa_per_play":0.174}],"comps":{"offense":[{"season":2022,"team":"IND","distance":0.4596,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Frank Reich"},{"season":2024,"team":"LV","distance":0.4777,"shared":12,"play_caller":null},{"season":2024,"team":"DAL","distance":0.4815,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Mike McCarthy"},{"season":2024,"team":"CLE","distance":0.495,"shared":12,"play_caller":null},{"season":2023,"team":"TB","distance":0.4985,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Dave Canales"}],"defense":[{"season":2022,"team":"CHI","distance":0.138,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2022,"team":"CIN","distance":0.1579,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Lou Anarumo"},{"season":2025,"team":"GB","distance":0.1785,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2025,"team":"BAL","distance":0.188,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2023,"team":"CIN","distance":0.2184,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Lou Anarumo"}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Texans are 2-4 through week 6 of the 2026 season and have outscored opponents 144 to 143. The offense has been carrying the team, ranking 12th in EPA per play while the defense sits 20th in EPA allowed.","offense":"The Texans offense has been a little above average by EPA per play so far, and it has been much better passing the ball than running it. Their run and pass mix has stayed close to what game situations call for. C.J. Stroud has run the passing game, with Dalton Schultz leading the team in targets.","defense":"The Texans defense has been a little below average by EPA allowed per play so far. Its strongest area has been success rate allowed, where it ranks 7th, and its weakest has been takeaways per game, where it ranks 20th. Danielle Hunter has led the way with 3 sacks. Their scheme has been fairly conventional, and the closest thing to a signature is a blitz rate that ranks 4th lowest in the league.","special":"The Texans have been about average in how often they go for it on fourth down. Their kickers have made 93% of field goals, which is well above average. On the roster side, they put an unusually large share of their salary cap into the defensive line, about 32% of the money on the books.","players":"C.J. Stroud has played nearly every snap at quarterback and thrown for 1,714 yards. Targets have been spread around, with Dalton Schultz and Xavier Hutchinson leading a group where nobody has more than a fifth of the looks. The backfield has been a committee led by Woody Marks and David Montgomery. On defense, Will Anderson leads the team with 7.5 sacks.","coaching":"Nick Caley is calling the offense and DeMeco Ryans is calling the defense. Their offense looks most like the 2022 Colts under Frank Reich and the 2024 Raiders. Their defense looks most like the 2022 Bears and the 2022 Bengals under Lou Anarumo.","trends":"The offense went from 21st in EPA per play in 2025 to 12th so far this season, a big step forward. The defense moved from 1st in EPA allowed per play in 2025 to 20th so far this season, a big step back. The biggest change in approach was two point attempt rate, which went from 17% to 0%.","notes":"The 2026 pages are built from data that nflverse updates every week, so they will keep changing until the season ends. Personnel, formations, coverage and pressure numbers are missing for now because that data is only released after the season."}}